{"name":"Silver Cross","hex":"#cdc5c2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Silver Cross","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high-level military service award.\n A Canadian award for those who died in active service, such as in combat","A Canadian award for those who died in active service, such as in combat"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Silver_Cross"}],"entries":[{"title":"South African Police Silver Cross for Gallantry","blocks":[{"text":"The South African Police Silver Cross for Gallantry was a decoration that existed between 1985 and 1989."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_African_Police_Silver_Cross_for_Gallantry","wikidata":"Q7565771"},{"title":"Memorial Cross","blocks":[{"text":"The Memorial Cross, often known as the Silver Cross for Mothers, is a Canadian decoration awarded to the mother, widow, widower, or next of kin of any member of the Canadian Armed Forces whose life is lost on active service, including peacekeeping, other such international operations and, since 2001, other service-related deaths."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/67/Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_V_version.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memorial_Cross","wikidata":"Q6815378"},{"title":"Silver Cross (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver Cross is an English private limited company and manufacturer of baby transport and other baby-related products, founded in 1877. Based in Skipton, North Yorkshire, United Kingdom, Silver Cross sells baby prams and pushchairs. Its parent company, the Chinese conglomerate Fosun International, owns 87.2 percent of the equity."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Cross_(company)","wikidata":"Q7515986"},{"title":"Cross","blocks":[{"text":"The cross is a geometrical figure consisting of two intersecting lines or bars, usually perpendicular to each other. The lines usually run vertically and horizontally. A cross of oblique lines, in the shape of the Latin letter X, is also termed a saltire in heraldic terminology. Throughout centuries the cross in its various shapes and forms was a symbol of various beliefs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Cross2.svg/330px-Cross2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross","wikidata":"Q40843"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version.jpg/120px-Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version.jpg/250px-Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version.jpg/120px-Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMemorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version_with_brooch.png/120px-Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version_with_brooch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version_with_brooch.png/250px-Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_version_with_brooch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Memorial_Cross%2C_Canada._King_George_VI_ver